+# Farm-box master: actual source and period comparison
+
+The licensed Old Cart by Lyskilde/longtail is the geometry, UV and PBR construction
+basis. Its unchanged original SHA256 is
+`13600b73c1777545e1454d452c58d141469f031b2c5e6c29b1c6fdefe9145046`.
+Actual source-native front, side and quarter images were inspected, alongside the
+new model views. The original's equal wheel sizes, paired shafts, bent front
+axle pose and raw proportions are deliberately changed to the reconstructed W01
+metre envelope. Weathered boards, iron rims, hubs, eight-spoke construction,
+joinery and material character remain the licensed artist's work. It is a modern
+construction reference; it identifies no historic maker, place or specimen.
+
+## Contemporary 1835 family-form cross-check
+
+John Caspar Wild, *Third and Vine Northside*, made 1835 and depicting 1835
+Cincinnati, Cincinnati Museum Center. Canonical record:
+`data/sources/wild_1835_third_vine.json`.
+Actual whole held image personally viewed 26 October 2026:
+`chicago/reference/images/cincinnati/cincinnati_wild_third_and_vine_1835.jpg`.
+SHA256: 428bfc9cf09352f3187fd31f6330310f64829fca17013b88de4ef812d37b966e.
+Its existing credit is in `chicago/reference/images/IMAGE_SOURCES.md`, under
+that exact filename: PD-Art / PD-old-100-expired, via Google Art Project / Commons.
+Source: https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_Caspar_Wild_-_Third_and_Vine_Northside_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg
+
+The lower-right wagon shows four spoked wheels, smaller front wheels, larger rear
+wheels, an upright-sided/staked work box and a canvas cover. These support the
+family and the differing front/rear-wheel reading used by the master. They do
+not supply recoverable metric dimensions, a confident spoke count, species,
+paint or underlying gear. The master deliberately has an open, empty box:
+canvas, cargo, horse, harness and driver are outside this ticket's one-master
+scope. Its weathered gray and optional warm timber are reconstructed alternatives;
+the painting's colored body is not reinterpreted as a record of our specimen.
+Cincinnati is not Chicago, and the depicted vehicle is not this vehicle.
+
+The reference permits a qualitative side/rear-quarter family comparison only.
+Its small painted wheels, canvas-hidden bed, unknown perspective and unknown
+scale cannot calibrate a unique optical camera, certify dimensions or support a
+pixel-perfect match. Current final-reach published side/quarter/close views are
+required for the actual model review; those captures are pending at this source
+checkpoint. No old pre-reach image qualifies the added coupling member.
+
+## Supplementary open-box analogue
+
+*The Eagle Tavern and Adjoining Buildings, 1825*, anonymous old print owned by
+the Buffalo Historical Society, reproduced in *The Picture Book of Earlier
+Buffalo* (1912), p. 163. This is an 1825 depicted scene; the underlying print's actual
+creation date is unknown within the 19th century. It is not called an 1825-made
+image. Actual held image viewed 26 October 2026:
+`chicago/reference/images/buffalo/buffalo_eagle_tavern_main_street_1825.jpg`.
+SHA256: 8499bfc6b3888f5b261fc5b69eb36876f19a6f383d9e528fe91d0861eadcbd69.
+The same committed catalogue records the 19th-century print and 1912 reproduction
+as public domain. Source: https://buffaloah.com/h/eagletav/index.html .
+
+The small wagon below and left of centre is an open four-wheel box carrying
+barrels. It supplies an independent illustrated open-box/load family comparison;
+its low-resolution halftone does not resolve joinery, kingbolt, reach, exact spoke
+count or material species. Cargo, occupants and teams are not added to this
+empty master. The print does not establish1835 Chicago presence, original
+coating color or a calibrated metric envelope.
+
+## Remaining limits and acceptance
+
+The modern source supplies surface detail; the dated and retrospective street
+views bound family plausibility. The master remains a labeled reconstruction.
+All body dimensions, steering range, independent wheel radii, central pole and
+reach engineering, colors, wear and proposed interfaces retain their explicit
+liberties. No new archive download, calibrated historical camera, hidden-feature
+attestation or photographic completion is claimed by this reference review.
+Existing 80 static wagons and the three fine-wood selections stay unchanged.
+Current published specimen views, measured browser costs, native repository
+checks and required whole-app renderer coverage remain distinct actual proofs.
